id: searx-changelog-migration
title: Migrate every existing changelog statement into pm-changelog source data
description: Preserve every existing released and Unreleased changelog statement as closed pm data and prove generated output loses nothing.
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 0
tags[4]: changelog,data-preservation,migration,pm-changelog
created_at: "2026-07-21T17:24:35.367Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-21T17:43:27.128Z"
deadline: "2026-07-23T17:24:35.367Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-21T17:43:26.241Z"
author: codex-root
acceptance_criteria: No existing changelog data is lost; release only occurs for release-relevant changes; exact package version is verified through npm and Bun
definition_of_ready: "Live pm, changelog, tags, package registry, GitHub secrets, and pm-cli workflow state inspected"
parent: searx-auto-release
risk: high
confidence: 90
sprint: 2026-07-release-automation
release: next
resolution: "Backfilled 19 historical entries, retained and corrected 12 pending entries, installed pm-changelog, and added a dual-source preservation gate."
expected_result: Every original statement remains present in pm and generated CHANGELOG.md with reachable historical release windows.
actual_result: Preservation reports 31 of 31 entries in both sources; pm-changelog check reports unchanged; legacy 2026.3.4-2 anomaly is explicitly retained in metadata.
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind}:
  searx-auto-release,related,"2026-07-21T17:24:35.367Z",codex-root,null
comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-21T17:24:35.367Z",codex-root,Work is governed by the lossless changelog and exact-version publishing acceptance gates.
  "2026-07-21T17:40:54.987Z",codex-root,Backfilled 19 historical statements and retained 12 existing pending statement items. Preservation check proves all 31 original entries exist in both pm and generated markdown.
  "2026-07-21T17:42:56.377Z",codex-root,"Direct workspace bun run changelog:pm:check passed with action=unchanged, changed=false, item_count=40; it is not linked through pm test because the pm sandbox intentionally excludes project node_modules required by the package peer."
notes[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-21T17:24:35.367Z",codex-root,Publish once to npm and verify the same package through both npm and Bun consumers.
  "2026-07-21T17:40:54.987Z",codex-root,The unreachable legacy 2026.3.4-2 heading is preserved as provenance metadata; generation maps its three statements to the real v2026.3.4 tag window.
learnings[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-21T17:24:35.367Z",codex-root,GitHub tag pushes made with GITHUB_TOKEN do not trigger downstream push workflows; production uses RELEASE_PAT.
  "2026-07-21T17:40:54.987Z",codex-root,Two prior pending items had dropped Markdown code spans; the preservation gate detected and corrected explorer.exe and E2E_SEARXNG_URL fidelity.
  "2026-07-21T17:42:56.377Z",codex-root,Tracker-reading commands need tracker pm_context; package-extension commands additionally require project dependency resolution and should be run directly or in a fully installed isolated clone.
files[3]{path,scope,note}:
  CHANGELOG.md,project,Generated release history
  scripts/release/check-changelog-preservation.mjs,project,Lossless migration gate
  scripts/release/changelog-baseline.json,project,31-entry pre-migration baseline
tests[1]{command,scope,timeout_seconds,pm_context_mode}:
  "bun run changelog:preservation:check",project,180,tracker
docs[1]{path,scope,note}:
  docs/release-process.md,project,Maintainer release documentation
close_reason: All 31 pre-migration changelog statements are represented in pm and retained by generated output.
body: Preserve every existing released and Unreleased changelog statement as closed pm data and prove generated output loses nothing.
